  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S1 is strict on reporting and customer notice. S2 is weakened by allowing sales up to a 10% failure rate and exempting existing models from the sales bar, though customers receive numeric rates and no public publication is required. S3 and S4 land in acceptable ranges (six-year retrofit, 36-month suppression), while S5 keeps the 8/100k mandatory recall but uses only 'promptly' notices and omits a serious-injury clause; overall the package favors Northwind."
